  "body": "Thanks for your excellent work!\n\nI have a question about the computation of the `aug_entropy_loss`, i.e. the part of the Double Entropy Regularization in the paper. The `aug_entropy_loss` is computed from `model_inputs[\"aug_log_probs\"]`, which is computed under the `torch.no_grad()` function `compute_log_prob`. That means no gradient will backward to the model, so maybe this loss is useless. And that's maybe why only using single entropy loss on the corrupted policy sequence does not prevent the collapse.\n\nMay I ask for your perspective on this matter?\n\nThanks.",
